Contents
  n48xlate/    a new crate: an in-process C ABI (cdylib libn48xlate.dylib) around the
               translator, so a sandboxed process can turn AIR text into SPIR-V without
               a helper daemon. New files; licence LGPL-3.0-or-later (SPDX headers).
  patches/     our changes to upstream's own files, as one diff per upstream base:
               0003 (on v2.7.2) applies to the tag and also adds the workspace root
               translator/Cargo.toml and the n48xlate crate; 0002 (on ceba63c) and
               0001 (on steelbrain 43c46ac) are kept for the bundles that used them.
  COPYING      the LGPL-3.0 text, as shipped by upstream.

How it is used: tools/native/navi48metal loads Resources/libn48xlate.dylib at run time
(tools/native/navi48metal/n48_xlate.h). No LGPL code is compiled or linked into the kext,
the Mesa patches or the MIT-licensed bundle sources; the library is a separate shared
object loaded dynamically. Anyone who builds and distributes libn48xlate.dylib must
follow the LGPL for that library and offer its source: the NullMoth tag above plus
patches/0003 (or ceba63c plus patches/0002 for bundles 29 to 35), including these changes.

No build outputs and no test data derived from Apple software are included. The test
programs in n48xlate/tests need a corpus directory you generate yourself
(N48X_CORPUS, see tests/corpus.rs); without it they do nothing and pass.
